Lanloom is made available so that people can run it to map their own home
network. It is source-available, NOT open-source: the source code is visible,
but the rights granted below are limited.

In short: private, non-commercial use with up to 100 devices is free of
charge. Private use with more devices, and every commercial use, requires a
separate paid license. The terms below are what counts.

DEFINITIONS
  • "Software" means Lanloom: its source code, container images, add-on,
    documentation and every update to them.
  • "Device" means each individual device or host, physical or virtual, that
    the Software discovers, lists or keeps in its inventory. Devices are
    counted together across all installations, sites and data folders of the
    Software that you run or use; the same device counts once. Devices of the
    built-in sample network do not count.
  • "Private Use" means use by one natural person for their own household, on
    machines that person owns or controls, that is not Commercial Use.
  • "Commercial Use" means any use by or on behalf of a company, a
    self-employed person, a public authority, an association, club or other
    organisation, or a school, university or other educational institution;
    any use by a service provider (including a managed service provider) for
    its customers or for anyone else; and any other use in connection with a
    trade, business, profession or other gainful activity. It does not matter
    whether the use itself earns money.

